            answer: 'A subsidy is a per-unit payment to producers or consumers of goods with positive externalities, designed to internalize the external benefit. The optimal subsidy equals the marginal external benefit (MEB) at the socially optimal output level Qs. The subsidy shifts the MPC curve downward by the subsidy amount, effectively reducing costs. After the subsidy, producers can supply at effective costs of MPC - subsidy. The new equilibrium occurs where MSB = (MPC - subsidy), achieving the socially optimal output at Qs instead of the lower free market output Qm. The subsidy incentivizes greater production/consumption by lowering the price faced by consumers from Pm to Pc, while producers receive Pp = Pc + subsidy. The quantity increases from Qm to Qs, eliminating the welfare loss from underproduction. The subsidy internalizes the positive externality by making producers/consumers consider the full social benefit.',
